    "author": null,
    "body": "# TPP10 domain survey and refinement handoff\n\nAuthorized work, 11 September 2026. Read Fieldbook experiment `exp_01m23ddmn78breygyvkkpzyrq8` first. Both submissions use central1-a, `gs://marin-us-central1`, 2 CPU / 8 GB on-demand coordinators, 48-hour deadlines and zero automatic coordinator retries. The Codex thread heartbeat `monitor-tpp10-domain-survey-and-refinement` checks every 15 minutes and reports actionable changes only.\n\n## New survey\n\nIris parent: `/calvinxu/tpp10-domain-sweeps`, submitted 11:08:39 UTC, explicit interactive priority. Fieldbook job `job_01m282e98jx2e0wv6p67gawx0p`. Frozen plan `30fc30f1a7e618900a2f1dc40fe5650237b06ea979f2cedfcf8ca664c496114b`.\n\nThe approved 28 points comprise Wikipedia/FineMath, target/matched proxy, p = 5, 10, 20, 30, 50, 70, 100%, trainer seed 20260910 and matched subset seed 20260912. Scale-specific p=0 checkpoints are reused. No unmatched arms, replicates, new StarCoder points, or automatic refinements. All seven Uncheatable components plus PALOMA are evaluated; selection uses the equal seven-component BPB mean. Target N=301,241,344/D=3,012,296,704, matched N=16,587,008/D=165,937,152; pools 190,316,544/10,485,760 tokens. Training budget 9.36434e19 FLOPs excludes prep/eval/compilation.\n\n`submitted_domain_sweeps.txt`, `plan.json`, `release.json` and `bundle_preflight.json` are the exact launch artifacts. The parent prepares two new finite pools (Wikipedia gzip and bounded FineMath3+ parquet), permutes their packed parent sequences and materializes one matched subset each. It verifies quotas/source generations/tokenizer/indices, actual allocator exposures and real finite evaluation tags before training. It runs the two matched p=100 points as included execution checks, requiring complete final checkpoints and all evaluation scores, then releases26 remaining points concurrently. Shared p=0 evaluations reuse the exact Figure5 namespace and can overlap with its queued evaluator; no training duplication. Regional token yield/decoder behavior remain runtime checks.\n\nNew code: `prepare_tpp10_domain_sweeps.py`, `launch_tpp10_domain_sweeps.py`, `analyze_tpp10_domain_sweeps.py`, new assets directory and `tests/test_tpp10_domain_sweeps.py`. Original StarCoder modules/assets and uv.lock must remain unchanged. CC review and follow-up are in this directory; `VALIDATION.md` records 18 passing tests, lint/typecheck, region and bundle checks. CC was invoked read-only via claude -p with ANTHROPIC_API_KEY removed. The TPU non-preemptible objection was withdrawn; only CPU coordinators/preparation are constrained on-demand, because central1 v5p is a preemptible pool. Children inherit the parent priority.\n\nDurable survey records: `gs://marin-us-central1/experiments/tpp10_domain_sweeps/30fc30f1a7e618900a2f1dc40fe5650237b06ea979f2cedfcf8ca664c496114b/`. `plan.json`, `release.json`, `preflight.json` are written after data preparation; `results.json` after all endpoints. Use the launcher --collect with the archived plan to collect completed full results. Report observed minima, actual epochs, neighboring losses, target loss at proxy choice and target-grid regret. Boundary minima do not establish turnover. No fitted curves or significance claims from one seed.\n\n## Refinement migration\n\nReplacement parent: `/calvinxu/starcoder-tpp10-refinement-batch`, submitted 11:09:27 UTC, explicit batch priority, Fieldbook job `job_01m282e9ktr05xrmj8d9p3tsxp`. Old parent `/calvinxu/starcoder-tpp10-refinement` was canceled only after checkpoint verification; the complete old tree was verified terminal and all 45 leases absent/expired before replacement.\n\nThe original plan `99ca724bc3bde33e80afb07373e47ddc0d7e44f22e15cd41da3daa3de2f4ef40` and all 45 fingerprints/outputs are unchanged: 40,55,60,65,80%, five targets/ten unmatched/thirty matched across the original seeds/subsets. Eleven successful artifacts are retained;34 unfinished recipes may run. Target p=55 has verified saved step 3010 metadata at the original temp-checkpoint path (see refinement_pre_migration.json); the launcher will resume the latest available checkpoint. No checkpoint deletion or forced data regeneration was done. Keep successful artifacts and source generation/index hashes intact.\n\n`submitted_refinement_batch.txt` carries the exact replacement command and includes the original release. `refinement_batch_reuse_audit.json` records all 45 output states/expired leases. Root CPU runtime and child TPU science remain unchanged. Stale RUNNING executor tokens are safe only because the corresponding old tree is terminal and leases expired; the native runner reacquires these leases. Do not delete lock files on live work.\n\n## Recovery and verification\n\nInspect Iris parent and child states, plus recent logs, not just a running root. Follow the Iris monitoring skill. Queueing is not a training failure. Use post_submission_status.json for the latest checked state, when present. Record state changes/retries and artifacts in Fieldbook and CC_CHANGES.md. Manual recovery is authorized within these frozen settings: first ensure old tree terminal and leases absent/expired, then rerun the same exact recipe/output identities, skipping verified successes. Keep new survey interactive and refinement batch. Never restart a cluster, raise user priority budgets, move data across regions, add experiments or duplicate training to escape a queue.\n\nPause the heartbeat after both authorized jobs and result verification complete. Manuscript and outline were not edited for this launch; CC should propagate scientific results once measured, not provisional minima.\n\n## Coordinator recovery at 11:18 UTC\n\nThe first all-batch replacement coordinator was scheduler-preempted by the interactive Wikipedia preparation job before dispatching training. It is superseded. Current refinement parent: `/calvinxu/starcoder-tpp10-refinement-batch-recovery`, submitted 11:18:27 UTC, Fieldbook job `job_01m28317ycr6k3vmhzm5xksec6`. The CPU coordinator is interactive; every TPU child is explicitly BATCH. This avoids sacrificing the entire sweep when individual batch training should yield capacity.\n\nThe new `resume_starcoder_tpp10_refinement_batch.py` wrapper changes only `JobRequest.priority` at dispatch via the native current-client context. It calls the frozen refinement launcher unchanged. The wrapper is separately pinned to SHA-256 `b99a6277374bb0da97a1df91b0fd7dad5a7f8f1004e33e224c5cf4bf571b1e84`; recovery bundle `3655dd72d95b64c91b0b39341b27308cead8f5a24402128694032f1390067246` verifies the original 28 pins plus the wrapper. CC found no blocker; lint and Pyrefly passed. All dependencies were already verified successful, so no CPU prep job should reach the wrapper's TPU-only dispatch guard. Region, parent resources, zero automatic retries, 45 scientific fingerprints and checkpoint paths are unchanged. Verify actual child priority from controller receipts once dispatch begins.\n\nUse `submitted_refinement_batch_recovery.txt` for any needed recovery, with a new documented parent attempt only after this tree is terminal and leases expired. Do not restart either superseded coordinator. Both original and first batch parents are terminal. Eleven completed training artifacts remain retained; the unfinished p=55 target can resume its saved checkpoint. The monitor now targets this recovery parent and the new domain survey.\n",
